Original commit body from 54a42e15ffe9dc76cc2523d1337915407dd180e8:

Scheme v9 promised that every enclosing scope that can repeat in a file is in
the hash. A post-merge live check found seven producers that hashed no parent
(markdown sections/code blocks/links, rst sections, scss nested rules, puppet
resources in classes, svelte template blocks, apex nested classes, fish nested
functions): the same construct under two different parents tied, the per-file
split pass ordered the twins, and deleting the first parent moved the second.
The floor gate passed because its fixtures held that shape for some languages
only. v9 is unreleased, so these fixes fold into it (no v10).

Producer fixes (all through the shared helpers: ancestor_labels,
make_doc_stable_id(scope=), scoped_stable_id, scoped_table_stable_id,
nested_qualified_name, nested_member_qualified_name):
- markdown: enclosing sections' titles (the grammar nests a section per level)
- rst: section hierarchy from adornment-style order (tree-sitter-rst emits
  sections as siblings; meta.level was always 1 and now reports the level)
- scss / puppet: rules, at-rules, classes, defines, nodes and branches
  (new base.block_prelude label: the text before a node's block)
- svelte / astro: element chain (new base.html_element_tag, shared with vue,
  which keeps byte-identical ids) plus svelte control-flow blocks
- apex: full enclosing type chain for nested types and their members
- fish: enclosing-function chain, as bash
Writing the two-parent fixtures found ten more: blade (open sections and
components), C (tags/typedefs/prototypes declared in a function; struct
nesting stays out, C11 6.2.1), CMake functions and macros in blocks, gnuplot
brace blocks (functions, variables, plots), HLSL namespaces/structs/functions
(c_family_scope_chain gains functions=/types=), JSON and Cargo dependency
groups, TOML 3+-part table names (the inner dotted_key was skipped, so
[tool.poetry.dependencies] and [target.'cfg(..)'.dependencies] were both
"dependencies"), Meson branches/loops, assembler local labels; and an else
labelled without its if (CMake, Meson, gnuplot; now the Makefile chain's
if/else shape). A Maven artifactId under two groupIds tied too (groupId
scope). Mermaid: a node id repeated in two subgraphs is one Mermaid node (a
documented same-scope tie); the same node in two diagrams already passed.

The structural guard (test_stable_id_floor_gate.py):
- SiblingCase.nested: one text, byte for byte, under two different parents,
  the first deleted. Same-scope copies tie, so a language is proved only when
  both copies emit the same kinds and the second keeps its ids
  (two_parent_languages).
- test_every_language_has_a_two_parent_fixture_or_is_flat: every language a
  fixture emits is proved, or listed in FLAT_LANGUAGES with a reason (24).
  "Nests" is not inferred from output alone (a markdown section spans its
  heading line; a Svelte element is no symbol), so the flat list is reviewed
  and fails as stale when the language's symbols nest (nesting_languages),
  when a fixture proves it, or when no fixture emits it.
- test_every_registered_language_has_a_fixture (yaml, html, play-routes
  exempt with reasons).
- 50 PARENT_CASES (49 two-parent, incl. three else-branch shapes, plus
  xml-maven); 46 existing fixtures gained nested= with identical copies.
  202 fixtures (95 two-parent), baseline still empty.
